"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["angular","javascript","pwa","typescript","web","web-framework","web-performance"],"visibility":"public","forks":27109,"open_issues":1141,"watchers":100153,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"**I'm submitting a ...**  (check one with \"x\")\n\n```\n[x] bug report => search github for a similar issue or PR before submitting\n[ ] feature request\n[ ] support request => Please do not submit support request here, instead see https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#question\n```\n\n**Current behavior** \nHaving following routes \nexport const routes: Routes = [\n       .........\n    path: 'order/:id', component: ExistingOrderComponent,\n    children: [\n        { path: '', redirectTo: 'summary', pathMatch: 'full' },\n        { path: 'summary', component: SummaryComponent},\n        { path: 'edit', component: EditComponent, canDeactivate: [CanDeactivateGuard]   }\n];\nCanDeactivateGuard is being activated on changing route between children nodes (eg: order/1/edit -> order/1/summary), but it doesn't when parent is changed (eg: order/1/edit -> order/2/edit)\n\n**Expected behavior**\nI think that CanDeactivateGuard set on a children segment has to be fired when its parent segment is changed and as it seems to me it has to be fired before parent's guard (if specified)\n\n**Reproduction of the problem**\ndemo of the problem is here http://plnkr.co/edit/4TT1iC?p=preview\n- **Angular version:** 2.0.0 and below\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/11664/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/an